HTTPS / SSL Integration (Security): Right now Nginx is serving traffic on HTTP (Port 80). For an ecommerce site, you must have HTTPS. We can automate Let's Encrypt / Certbot within our Docker Compose setup to give you a free, auto-renewing SSL certificate. (Note: You need a registered Domain Name pointing to your EC2 IP for this).
Distributed Caching (Redis): We can introduce a Redis container into the docker-compose.yml and wire up the API to cache high-traffic endpoints (like the Product Catalog) or store Shopping Cart sessions, massively improving performance.
Background Jobs (Hangfire): If you need to send order confirmation emails, process refunds, or clean up abandoned carts without slowing down the user's web request, we can implement a robust background job processor.
Stripe Webhooks: If you want to securely handle payment completions asynchronously, we can build out the Stripe webhook listener endpoints.